    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! All tests are now passing. Here's what I fixed:\n\n**Issue 1 - governance.test.js**: The test was trying to import `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export, but it wasn't being exported from `src/finetune/index.js`. I added named exports for the constants that were being imported from the schema.\n\n**Issue 2 - eval/index.test.js**: The `toxicityMetric` function only takes outputs as its first parameter (with optional custom banned terms), but `runEvaluations` was calling all metrics with both outputs and references. This caused the references to be treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging safe content. I fixed it by checking the function's arity (`metric.length`) to determine whether to pass one or two parameters\u2014functions with only one required parameter now get just the outputs.\n\nAll 28 tests across 8 test files now pass. \u2713",
